{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Latch, timer, and sampler",
  "exampleId": "block-latch-timer",
  "description": "Start is pressed at 0.5 s and Stop at 1.5 s. Their rising edges set and reset the RS flip-flop, so Running is true from 0.5 s to 1.5 s. The timer counts seconds while Running is true. The logic switch passes the sine only while running and 0 otherwise. The triggered sampler reads the clock on the start edge and holds 0.5. Enable is a Boolean constant ANDed with Start: set it to false and nothing starts.",
